ric Inequalities , Titu Andreescu and Oleg Mushkarov\n* Number Theory Concepts and Problems , Titu Andreescu, Gabriel Dospinescu, and Oleg Mushkarov\n* A Romanian Problem Book , Titu Andreescu and Marian Tetiva\n* Graphs , Radu Bumbacea\n* Balkan Mathematical Olympiads , Mircea Becheanu and Bogdan Enescu\n* Cuban Mathematical Olympiads,  Robert Bosch (translated by Enrique Treviño--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNumber Theory: Concepts and Problems | Mathematical Association of America (https://old.maa.org/node/996060)\nciteturn608search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.0 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; Titu Andreescu, Gabriel Dospinescu, and Oleg MushkarovPublisher: ... Problem Book ... This one, however, is something of an exception, and stands out more vividly from the crowd, both because of its heft (at almost 700 pages, it is quite thick) and, more significantly, because of its content: in addition to setting out problems and solutions, it actually develops a substantial amount of elementary undergraduate number theory, and therefore seems more textbook-oriented than many other problem-style books.\n\n# Number Theory: Concepts and Problems\n\nImage\n\n###### \n\nTitu Andreescu, Gabriel Dospinescu, and Oleg Mushkarov\n\nPublisher: \n\nXYZ Press\n\nPublication Date: \n\n2017\n\nNumber of Pages: \n\n686\n\nFormat: \n\nHardcover\n\nPrice: \n\n79.95\n\nISBN: \n\n9780988562202\n\nCategory: \n\nProblem Book\n\n  * MAA Review\n  * Table of Contents\n\n[Reviewed by\n\nMark Hunacek\n\n, on\n\n10/12/2017\n\n]\n\nXYZ Press is a small publishing company whose books are distributed by the American Mathematical Society, and which specializes in texts that are designed to teach mathematical problem solving and competition preparation. It was established by Titu Andreescu, who is also the editor, author or co-author of many of the roughly two dozen texts published by this company, including the one now under review, which deals with problems in number theory.\n\nI have seen a good many problem books over the years, and must admit that after a while many of them tend to blur together in my mind. This one, however, is something of an exception, and stands out more vividly from the crowd, both because of its heft (at almost 700 pages, it is quite thick) and, more significantly, because of its content: in addition to setting out problems and solutions, it actually develops a substantial amount of elementary undergraduate number theory, and therefore seems more textbook-oriented than many other problem-style books. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReferences\n\n[1] Adler, I., *A New Look at Geometry (https://preparamates.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Complex-Numbers-www.preparamates.com_.pdf)\nciteturn608search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.7 years ago; [7] Andreescu, T., Dospinescu, G., *Straight from the Book*, XYZ Press, Dallas, 2012.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStraight From the Book by Titu Andreescu; Gabriel Dospinescu: As New Hardcover (2012) 1st Edition | BookManBookWoman Books (https://www.abebooks.com/first-edition/Straight-Book-Titu-Andreescu-Gabriel-Dospinescu/31067112227/bd)\nciteturn608search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; ### Items related to Straight From the Book ... ## Titu Andreescu; Gabriel Dospinescu ... Publisher ... Much of his career has been devoted to competition math, an efficient medium for teaching creative problem-solving for a wide-range of math topics.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVolume 8, No. 1, Spring 2021                                                                 79 (https://amj-math.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/AMJ2021-vol8iss1.pdf)\nciteturn608search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.2 years ago; Finally, after developing an inequality or applying an external fact from number th